                <pb facs="1034" n="1024" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1024"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12–2845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Robertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-28T14:00:00+07:00">December 28,
                            1945—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:14 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2232. According to telegram dated December 26 from Ward, Ining delegates arrived
                    at Tihwa, December 25. (Embtel 2139, December 11 to Dept repeated Moscow.) Ward
                    states delegates’ attitude <pb facs="1035" n="1025" xml:id="pg1025"/> said to be
                    conciliatory and friendly. (Sent Dept, repeated Moscow.) Chiang Ching-kuo,
                    Generalissimo’s son, was due at Tihwa, December 26 or 27, Ward stated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
